# Point of Checkout (pos) System - Implementation Plan

> **A dedicated touch-optimized Point-of-Sale application for in-store retail operations**

---

## Overview

This plan outlines the implementation of a comprehensive **Point of Checkout (pos)** system for Infi Commerce. The pos will be a **separate Next.js application** built specifically for in-store sales, featuring touch optimization, barcode scanning, quick checkout, and receipt printing capabilities.

---

## Architecture Decision

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "🏪 Store Environment"
        pos[pos App - Touch Optimized]
        Scanner[Barcode Scanner]
        Printer[Receipt Printer]
    end
    
    subgraph "⚡ Backend API"
        API[Express.js Backend]
        Auth[Store Admin Auth]
    end
    
    subgraph "🖥️ Admin Panel"
        Admin[Next.js Admin]
        BarcodeGen[Barcode Generator]
        posSettings[pos Settings]
    end
    
    subgraph "🗄️ Database"
        DB[(MongoDB)]
    end
    
    pos <--> API
    Scanner --> pos
    pos --> Printer
    Admin <--> API
    API <--> DB
```

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Separate Application vs Embedded in Admin**
> - The pos will be a **standalone Next.js application** in `/pos` directory
> - This provides touch-optimized UI, dedicated UX, and isolation from admin panel
> - Alternative: Could be a route inside admin panel, but touch optimization would be harder

> [!CAUTION]
> **Receipt Printer Selection**
> - Thermal printer support requires selection of printer SDK (e.g., ESC/POS, Star WebPRNT, EPSON ePOS)
> - Default: Web-based receipt printing via browser print API
> - Hardware: Need user confirmation on printer model/SDK preference

> [!WARNING]
> **Barcode Format**
> - Proposed: Use SKU-based **Code 128** or **EAN-13** format
> - Confirm preferred barcode format and label specifications

